Source: https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/rsync
Commit: 13eacd7e9a204b236310dab23682f6354ecc69bd (rsync-184)
Directory: openrsync/
License: ISC and the other notices retained in the source and LICENSE.md.

The rsync implementation is built as a static library in bx. The applet entry
point is bx_rsync_main in main.c. The Meson build runs Apple's
compile/link-only feature probes out of tree. Build the applet through the
root Meson project; there is no separate rsync build.

Local changes to Apple's files:
- Shared bx text buffers for sbuf storage and unit labels for human-readable
  formatting outside FreeBSD.
- Shared bx permission formatting, retaining rsync's trailing space.
- BX option scanning for client, daemon startup and daemon peer arguments.
- Portable socket lengths, FTS and queue handling.
- Confined opens use the shared bx resolution primitive on Linux and FreeBSD;
  platforms without a suitable primitive return ENOTSUP.
- The bx applet re-executes its own verified executable descriptor for
  local transfers. Remote transfers still default to the remote rsync.
- Nonlocal symbols are namespaced in bx to avoid clashes with other libraries.
- Compression uses the shared system zlib dependency. Matched blocks update
  the raw-deflate dictionaries with deflateSetDictionary and
  inflateSetDictionary, without passing matched data through the codec.
  Both retain protocol 29's repeated-prefix history for large matched blocks.
- The generated FTS fallback declarations are inside the config header guard.
- The metadata permission mask uses the standard mode bits on systems without
  ALLPERMS.
- Apple-private tracing is optional when its SDK header is unavailable.

This is openrsync, not a GNU rsync CLI clone.
